{#
    The Pi's complete Caddy config, templated by deploy_caddy.py as the
    single declarative source of truth (ADR-0008) -- nothing is ever
    hand-edited on the device. This is the templated evolution of
    services/auto_wake_proxy/Caddyfile (built by
    .scratch/homelab-control-system/issues/05-auto-wake-proxy.md): the
    wake_on_lan mechanism below is ported from that file. See that file's
    README (services/auto_wake_proxy/README.md) for the full plugin
    research/rationale and live-verification writeup behind the
    wake_on_lan mechanism -- not repeated here to avoid two copies of the
    same argument drifting out of sync.

    Requires a Caddy binary built with github.com/dulli/caddy-wol
    compiled in (see services/auto_wake_proxy/README.md's Build section);
    that build step is not this ticket's concern.

    Per ADR-0011, this file carries no per-workload knowledge -- everything
    under /server is forwarded, path-stripped, to a single fixed upstream
    on the main server. Which path reaches which Docker service (Immich,
    AI agents, etc.) is decided entirely by a reverse proxy running on
    that server itself, not templated here.

    Deliberately does NOT proxy to the Control server API: the browser
    calls it directly at its own tailscale-served origin (ADR-0001, "no
    Pi-side relay"). The Control UI is built (deploy_control_pi_api.py)
    with VITE_CONTROL_SERVER_API_URL pointing at that real origin, so the
    client -- not this Caddy instance -- is what "routes to" the Control
    server API.
#}
{
	order wake_on_lan before respond

	# ADR-0004 hard requirement: never bound off-tailnet. An external
	# `tailscale serve` instance is expected to front this Caddy, exactly
	# as control_pi_api/control_server_api's own bind_host convention
	# (services/shared/src/control_plane_shared/bind_safety.py).
	default_bind {$AUTO_WAKE_PROXY_BIND_HOST:127.0.0.1}
}

# --- Reusable auto-wake route -------------------------------------------
# One snippet, imported below. {args[0]} is the upstream address (host:port)
# to proxy to.
(auto_wake_route) {
	reverse_proxy {args[0]} {
		lb_try_duration 3s
		lb_try_interval 500ms
	}

	handle_errors {
		@server_asleep expression {err.status_code} == 502
		handle @server_asleep {
			wake_on_lan {$SERVER_MAC_ADDRESS} {$WOL_BROADCAST_ADDRESS:255.255.255.255:9}

			reverse_proxy {args[0]} {
				lb_try_duration 120s
				lb_try_interval 1s
			}
		}
	}
}

# --- Single site: Control UI, Control Pi API, and the main server --------
# One origin, path-routed. `/wake` reaches the Control Pi API; everything
# else falls through to the Control UI's static files, except `/server`,
# which is forwarded (path stripped) to the main server as a single blind
# upstream (ADR-0011) -- this Caddy has no opinion on what's behind it.
:{{ control_ui_port }} {
	handle /wake* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{{ control_pi_api_port }}
	}

	handle_path /server* {
		import auto_wake_route {{ main_server_host }}:{{ server_proxy_port }}
	}

	handle {
		root * {{ control_ui_root }}
		file_server
	}
}
